      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Stress can certainly lead to intense headaches, including tension headaches which may seem overpowering but are typically less intense than migraines. Over-the-counter medications like ibuprofen might help, but please monitor the intensity and duration of your pain. If the pain does not subside with over-the-counter medication and is accompanied by other symptoms like nausea, visual disturbances, or if it significantly interferes with your daily activities, it's essential to consider getting medical advice.\n\nIf you are sure that you're in a non-emergency situation, sometimes calling a local clinic or scheduling an online appointment can save you time. Take extra care of yourself, especially given the stress you’re under. Remember, seeking professional help early can make a difference in outcomes. Swallowing your concerns and prioritizing your health now could save you from more problems later.",
